# ABSOLUTE RULE: NEVER ASSUME — VERIFY EVERYTHING

**This is the single most important rule in this project. It overrides all other priorities
except "don't break production." No deadline, no convenience, no "I'm pretty sure" justifies
skipping verification. If you violate this rule, the code you produce is worthless.**

## The Core Principle

**You do not know anything until you have verified it.** Your training data is stale. Your
"intuition" about this codebase is pattern-matching that produces confident-sounding garbage.
Every time you think "I'm pretty sure this field exists" or "this probably works like X," you
are about to write a bug.

The antidote is simple: **look before you leap.** You have access to the codebase, the schema,
the logs, and the user. Use them.

